  "payload": {
   "provider": "Dr. Paul Meadows",
   "specialty": "endocrinology",
   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Ray-Scott Clinic\nPatient: Adam Yu DOB: 12/05/1980 Sex: M MRN: 593664\n\nEncounters:\n 2024-07-28 lab review BP 133/90 Wt 169\n 2024-03-21 Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose BP 140/82 Wt 165\n 2023-11-12 Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose BP 129/83 Wt 170\n 2023-07-05 ankle sprain BP 136/79 Wt 2023-02-25 Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose BP 137/82 Wt 178\n 2022-10-19 Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose BP 133/83 Wt 172\n 2022-06-11 Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose BP 139/90 Wt 179\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Prediabetes / impaired fasting glucose (A1c 5.4) - controlled; meds: metformin 1000 mg\n A1C trend: 07/24 5.2, 03/24 5.4, 11/23 5.4, 07/23 5.6\n Patient has been consistent in monitoring his blood glucose levels and dietary intake, as well as incorporating regular exercise into his routine. His latest A1C result of 5.2 is a testament to his commitment to managing his prediabetic state.\n • Vitals stable; latest BP 133/90, weight 169 lbs\n Blood pressure readings have remained within a normal range, and weight has been steadily decreasing. This is a positive sign for overall metabolic health.\n • Social history: consumes approximately 12 alcoholic per week\n No significant changes in his alcohol consumption pattern, which remains moderate limits. However, ongoing monitoring is advised to ensure it does not escalate.\n\nAdditional Clinical Notes:\nAdam Yu is a 43-year-old male who has been under our care since 2016 for the management of prediabetes, specifically impaired fasting glucose. His A1C levels have been carefully monitored over the years, with values showing a gradual improvement.\n\nOn 07/28/2024, Adam presented for a routine lab review. His blood pressure was recorded at 133/90, and weight was 169 pounds. His A1C at this visit was 5.2, indicating stable glycemic control. Metformin 1000 mg daily remains his sole medication, which he has been taking consistently.\n\nAdam's exercise regimen includes running 3-4 times a week, contributing positively to his overall health and weight management. His diet has been well-controlled, supporting his efforts to manage prediabetes effectively.\n\nOn 03/21/2024, Adam visited for a follow-up on his prediabetic condition. His blood pressure was 140/82, and he weighed 165 pounds. His A1C at this visit was 5.4, reflecting a steady trend.\n\nFurther back, on 11/12/2023, he presented again for prediabetes management. His blood pressure was 129/83, and weight 170 pounds. His A1C was 5.4, consistent with previous measurements.\n\nOn 07/05/2"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "023, Adam visited due to an ankle sprain. His blood pressure was 136/79, and he weighed 181 pounds at the time. No significant changes were noted in his prediabetic management during this visit.\n\nOn 02/25/2023, Adam's prediabetes management continued with a blood pressure of 137/82 and weight 178 pounds. His A1C at this visit was 5.6, slightly elevated from previous readings but still within the controlled range.\n\nOn 10/19/2022, his blood pressure was 133/83, and he weighed 172 pounds. His A1C at this visit was 5.4, indicating stable control.\n\nFinally, on 06/11/2022, Adam's blood pressure was 139/90, and he weighed 179 pounds. His A1C at this visit was 5.6, showing a slight fluctuation but overall stable management.\n\nFamily History:\nAdam's mother passed away from colon cancer at age 57, having been diagnosed at age 47. His father had hypertension, diagnosed at age 65, and passed away at age 83.\n\nOverall, Adam Yu demonstrates a proactive approach to managing his prediabetes with lifestyle modifications and medication adherence. His continued commitment to a healthy lifestyle and regular monitoring is commendable. We anticipate continued stable management of his condition.\n"
    }
   ],
